# Homesync

Catalog + selective materialization (not full-mirror sync).

- Linux owns blobs; SQLite owns identity, tags, provenance, per-device availability.
- Phone modes: `listed` | `cached` | `pinned`. Listed ≠ full bytes.
- Identity: `file_id` + `content_hash`. Paths are attributes.
- v1 conflicts: LWW metadata; never merge divergent blobs.
- Soft deletes / tombstones; GC only when unreferenced.
- Read `AGENTS.md` and `docs/` before changing architecture.
- Do not commit unless asked. Do not expose daemon on hostile nets without auth.
